// Rules qcc owns, reported by qcc, at a Mojo column.
//
// These programs are valid Mojo: the fork registers the PrelimHLEP dialect
// but stubs its verifiers, because quantum semantics are qcc's to check, once.
// The locations Mojo wrote into the IR are what makes the diagnostic land on
// the line the user wrote.
//
// REQUIRES: mojo-kernels
// RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
// RUN: %kgen --elaborate -O1 --emit-quantum-kernels=%t %mojo_kernels/errors/leak.mojo
// RUN: not qcc --frontend=mojo-ir --compile-to=mlir %t/leak.mlir 2>&1 \
// RUN:     | FileCheck --check-prefix=LEAK %s
// RUN: %kgen --elaborate -O1 --emit-quantum-kernels=%t %mojo_kernels/errors/bad_basis.mojo
// RUN: not qcc --frontend=mojo-ir --compile-to=mlir %t/bad_basis.mlir 2>&1 \
// RUN:     | FileCheck --check-prefix=BASIS %s

// A variable assigned inside a linearization body and read after it. Mem2Reg
// cannot promote it -- what a body writes does not leave it -- so it survives
// as memory, and the memory op is what qcc has to name.
// LEAK: leak.mojo:14:9: error: 'pop.stack_allocation' is not supported in a quantum kernel: a value assigned inside a linearization body cannot be read after it; results leave a body through 'prelimhlep.output'
// LEAK: var leaked = False

// An X-basis constant that is not one: caught by qcc's verifier, printed at
// the Mojo line that wrote it.
// BASIS: bad_basis.mojo:21:14: error: 'prelimhlep.constant' op expected only '+'/'-' symbols for result type '!prelimhlep.lin<!prelimhlep.x<1>>', got '?'
